{"name":"Burning Bush","hex":"#a0403e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burning bush","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A biblical object described in Exodus 3:1-22, used by Yahweh to communicate with Moses.","Any plant of several species of Euonymus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burning_bush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Burning bush","blocks":[{"text":"The burning bush refers to an event recorded in the Jewish Torah. It happened in the mid-15th century BCE or the 13th century BCE. It is described in the third chapter of the Book of Exodus as having occurred on Mount Horeb. According to the biblical account, the bush was on fire but was not consumed by the flames, hence the name. In the biblical and Quranic narrative, the burning bush is the location at which Moses was appointed by God to lead the Israelites out of Egypt and into Canaan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg/330px-Bourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_bush"},{"title":"Burning Bush (miniseries)","blocks":[{"text":"Burning Bush is a 2013 three-part miniseries created for HBO by Polish director Agnieszka Holland. Based on real characters and events, this haunting drama focuses on the personal sacrifice of a Prague history student, Jan Palach, who set himself on fire in 1969 in protest against the Soviet occupation of Czechoslovakia in the previous year. Dagmar Burešová, a young female lawyer, became part of his legacy by defending Palach's family in a trial against the communist government, a regime which tried to dishonour Palach’s sacrifice, a heroic action for the freedom of Czechoslovakia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/64/Burning_Bush_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_Bush_(miniseries)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg/500px-Bourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg/500px-Bourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Burning Bush. Seventeenth-century painting by Sébastien Bourdon in the Hermitage Museum, Saint Petersburg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Moses_Dura_Europos.jpg/330px-Moses_Dura_Europos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Moses_Dura_Europos.jpg/330px-Moses_Dura_Europos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Moses and the burning bush. Painting from Dura-Europos synagogue, third century CE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoses_Dura_Europos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Bouts_moses.jpg/500px-Bouts_moses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Bouts_moses.jpg/1280px-Bouts_moses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Bouts_moses.jpg/500px-Bouts_moses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Moses and the Burning Bush, c. 1450–1475, attributed to Dieric Bouts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABouts_moses.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/